{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtPR7iahrZocYYGVUCRF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The architecture is Gemma 3 270M: 18 layers, hidden size 640, 4 query heads sharing 1 KV head (head_dim 256), a GeGLU MLP with 2048 units, and Gemma's sandwich norms. Full attention is used at layers 5, 11 and 17.\n\nNext I want per-tensor difference statistics: the relative Frobenius norm of A−B, the fraction of elements that are bitwise identical, and the effective rank of the difference. These show where the fine-tunes diverge and whether the training was LoRA (low-rank difference, rank ≤ 2r) or full fine-tuning. Both hypotheses predict the same pattern here, so this step is about locating the difference, not its direction.\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\ncA, cB = Checkpoint(\"A\"), Checkpoint(\"B\")\nrows=[]\nfor k in cA.keys():\n    a=cA.get(k); b=cB.get(k); d=a-b\n    rel=np.linalg.norm(d)/ (np.linalg.norm(a)+1e-12)\n    same=(d==0).mean()\n    r=\"\"\n    if d.ndim==2:\n        s=np.linalg.svd(d,compute_uv=False)\n        e=s**2/ (s**2).sum()\n        r=f\"top5 energy {e[:5].round(3)} n90={np.searchsorted(np.cumsum(e),0.9)+1}\"\n    rows.append((k,rel,same,np.linalg.norm(d),r))\nfor k,rel,same,dn,r in rows:\n    print(f\"{k:55s} rel={rel:.4f} same={same:.3f} |d|={dn:.4f} {r}\")\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8281,"cache_read_input_tokens":2942,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8281},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"912730f0-6d69-4509-908c-fe9b8d112f23","uuid":"8bd7d145-3880-43e2-91be-0611d353e41a","timestamp":"2026-11-10T01:34:14.075Z","request_id":"req_011CgtPR7aepRRsunfxtNtue"}
